00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:11.147
There are four levels of learning.

00:04:11.147 --> 00:04:12.915
Okay, let me tell you what the levels are.

00:04:12.915 --> 00:04:14.458
Some of you might now,
because you've been through

00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:16.088
any self-development, this
is some very basic stuff,

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.121
but it's important here.

00:04:17.121 --> 00:04:21.288
The first level is called being
unconsciously incompetent.

00:04:22.162 --> 00:04:23.397
And what that means is this.

00:04:23.397 --> 00:04:26.131
When you first start doing something

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:29.099
you know so little about it,
you basically know nothing.

00:04:29.099 --> 00:04:31.609
You don't know what you don't know.

00:04:31.609 --> 00:04:33.413
This is a very scary spot to be in,

00:04:33.413 --> 00:04:34.895
when you're thrown into a situation

00:04:34.895 --> 00:04:36.927
and you're a complete novice.

00:04:36.927 --> 00:04:38.717
You say, "Jeez, I'd love
to get better at this,

00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:41.543
"but I haven't the slightest
idea what I don't know."

00:04:41.543 --> 00:04:43.021
Everyone follow that concept?

00:04:43.021 --> 00:04:44.949
This is where most people start off, okay?

00:04:44.949 --> 00:04:49.584
The next level is becoming
consciously incompetent.

00:04:49.584 --> 00:04:51.001
That means that you're like,

00:04:51.001 --> 00:04:53.901
"Jesus Christ, I don't know anything."

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.526
You're like, "There's this,
there's that, there's that,

00:04:55.526 --> 00:04:56.554
"there's all these strategies.

00:04:56.554 --> 00:04:57.387
"They all sound great.

00:04:57.387 --> 00:04:58.383
"I don't know them."

00:04:58.383 --> 00:05:00.577
That's the next level.

00:05:00.577 --> 00:05:04.744
Next level above that is called
being consciously competent.

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:10.912
Consciously competent means
that you're good at something,

00:05:10.912 --> 00:05:13.768
but you can't really do it
with your eyes closed yet.

00:05:13.768 --> 00:05:16.055
You're good, but it
requires all your focus

00:05:16.055 --> 00:05:17.285
and your mental energy.

00:05:17.285 --> 00:05:19.317
Like, remember when we
were kids growing up,

00:05:19.317 --> 00:05:20.371
learning to tie your shoe?

00:05:20.371 --> 00:05:23.126
In the beginning, you're
like tie your shoe like.

00:05:23.126 --> 00:05:24.205
You're puttinh your things across,

00:05:24.205 --> 00:05:25.853
and someone says, "Excuse me."

00:05:25.853 --> 00:05:27.792
You're like, "Don't interrupt me!"

00:05:27.792 --> 00:05:28.863
You can't tie your shoe,

00:05:28.863 --> 00:05:31.327
and have a conversation at the same time.

00:05:31.327 --> 00:05:32.371
Right?

00:05:32.371 --> 00:05:34.826
That's when you're consciously
competent in something.

00:05:34.826 --> 00:05:37.716
It requires all your conscious focus.

00:05:37.716 --> 00:05:40.315
The next level above that

00:05:40.315 --> 00:05:43.565
is called being unconscious competence.

00:05:44.546 --> 00:05:46.126
And that means when you're really, really

00:05:46.126 --> 00:05:49.679
great at something, you can do
it without thinking about it.

00:05:49.679 --> 00:05:54.550
And the only way to get
from conscious competence,

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.513
to unconscious competence
is through practice.

00:05:58.513 --> 00:05:59.955
There's no other way.

00:05:59.955 --> 00:06:04.283
By drilling it into your head,
again, and again, and again,

00:06:04.283 --> 00:06:08.153
and again, and again, until
your brain just clicks,

00:06:08.153 --> 00:06:09.488
and all of a sudden you're using

00:06:09.488 --> 00:06:11.631
the unconscious part of your mind,

00:06:11.631 --> 00:06:14.302
which is infinitely more powerful

00:06:14.302 --> 00:06:15.913
than your conscious mind.

00:06:15.913 --> 00:06:19.844
The reason that most
people are not successful,

00:06:19.844 --> 00:06:23.197
or not wealthy, is not
because they set their goals

00:06:23.197 --> 00:06:25.114
too high and miss them.

00:06:27.347 --> 00:06:31.264
It's 'cause they set them
too low and hit them.

00:06:32.127 --> 00:06:33.540
Get that?

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.088
It's not because you set
your goals too high and miss.

00:06:36.088 --> 00:06:39.481
You set your goals too
low and you hit them.

00:06:39.481 --> 00:06:41.860
And you get caught up in
the average daily struggle

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.312
of averages and mediocrity.

00:06:44.312 --> 00:06:45.491
That's what kills people.

00:06:45.491 --> 00:06:47.517
Everybody raise your hand
for a second, please.

00:06:47.517 --> 00:06:48.813
Raise your hand.

00:06:48.813 --> 00:06:50.763
Now raise it as high as you can.

00:06:50.763 --> 00:06:53.070
I'm going to crouch so I can see, okay?

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:55.420
Now just raise it a bit
higher, everyone, higher.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.200
Why the hell did that happen?

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.573
I say, "Raise it as high as you can."

00:06:59.573 --> 00:07:00.406
And everyone says, "All right."

00:07:00.406 --> 00:07:01.239
Then, "A little bit higher."

00:07:01.239 --> 00:07:03.055
"Okay, well if you really mean it," right?

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.531
You get it?

00:07:04.531 --> 00:07:09.166
It's that extra inch, that's
where you want to set your goal.

00:07:09.166 --> 00:07:11.507
Not pie-in-the-sky and out of control,

00:07:11.507 --> 00:07:12.670
like it's never going to happen.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:13.835
'Cause that's a load of crap, too.

00:07:13.835 --> 00:07:15.778
People that set those sort of goals,

00:07:15.778 --> 00:07:18.315
they abandon those goals,
and we'll get to that later.

00:07:18.315 --> 00:07:20.697
But the idea here is,
you want to set the goals

00:07:20.697 --> 00:07:23.114
just above your comfort zone.

00:07:24.998 --> 00:07:26.281
So now, think about it for a second.

00:07:26.281 --> 00:07:27.966
Think about your goals right now.

00:07:27.966 --> 00:07:28.799
How do you set 'em?

00:07:28.799 --> 00:07:32.013
Are you setting them very
low and hitting them?

00:07:32.013 --> 00:07:34.066
If that's the case,
then give yourself a 10.

00:07:34.066 --> 00:07:36.430
Are you setting goals
that don't inspire you?

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.070
Some people set goals that might be high,

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:40.041
but they're crappy goals.

00:07:40.041 --> 00:07:41.349
They're not the sort of
goals that make you jump

00:07:41.349 --> 00:07:43.107
out of bed in the morning.

00:07:43.107 --> 00:07:45.815
Make you want to go to work for yourself.

00:07:45.815 --> 00:07:47.184
To secure the future, not just for you,

00:07:47.184 --> 00:07:48.536
but for your family.

00:07:48.536 --> 00:07:51.747
So you don't have to compromise
or acquiesce to anybody,

00:07:51.747 --> 00:07:54.009
unless you love them, unless you want to.

00:07:54.009 --> 00:07:54.842
That's freedom.

00:07:54.842 --> 00:07:57.889
You know, money's just a
mechanism to get there.

00:07:57.889 --> 00:08:00.712
Most people, and here's the
irony, is that most people

00:08:00.712 --> 00:08:04.332
don't have a compelling
vision for their own future.

00:08:04.332 --> 00:08:05.165
They don't.

00:08:05.165 --> 00:08:07.549
They move through life setting goals,

00:08:07.549 --> 00:08:08.832
and goals have no power.

00:08:08.832 --> 00:08:13.102
Goals had power in 1959,
when Earl Nightingale came

00:08:13.102 --> 00:08:14.572
to this idea of goal-setting,
and everyone was like,

00:08:14.572 --> 00:08:15.998
"Wow, I'm a goal-oriented person."

00:08:15.998 --> 00:08:17.536
And that was great, and it
worked for like 20 years.

00:08:17.536 --> 00:08:19.469
Everyone set goals, and they got results.

00:08:19.469 --> 00:08:21.850
But then all of a sudden,
you set goals, and sometimes

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:22.975
you hit them, sometimes you don't.

00:08:22.975 --> 00:08:26.240
Most times you don't, and
that's okay, but goals almost

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:29.017
became a synonym for like,
"Oh, I'm going to set a goal,

00:08:29.017 --> 00:08:30.667
"and who gives a (bleep) what
really happens afterwards."

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:33.088
It almost is synonymous with
failure now, goal-setting.

00:08:33.088 --> 00:08:35.812
And I believe in setting
goals, but there's got to

00:08:35.812 --> 00:08:37.722
be something above your goals.

00:08:37.722 --> 00:08:41.157
And that's your vision for the future.

00:08:41.157 --> 00:08:42.372
It doesn't have an ending point.

00:08:42.372 --> 00:08:45.150
It's about the world being a certain way.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.224
And that's inspiring to you.

00:08:47.224 --> 00:08:49.478
When you truly have a
vision for your future

00:08:49.478 --> 00:08:52.027
that inspires you, you're
going to jump up out of bed

00:08:52.027 --> 00:08:54.824
